CloudBurrow patch 21 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1202). Applies after patch 0020.

The bug: a column cast to STRING at run time was written with the value's
ToString, which is the wire form, not BigQuery's CAST form. The analyzer
folds a cast of a literal with BigQuery's own code, so a literal and a
column of the same value gave different strings. Measured with patches
0001 to 0020, column against literal:
- DATETIME: "2018-12-03T15:30:00" against "2018-12-03 15:30:00", and
  sub-second digits "...00.5" against "...00.500";
- TIME: "15:30:00.5" against "15:30:00.500";
- FLOAT64: "NaN", "+Inf", "-Inf" against "nan", "inf", "-inf";
- BYTES: base64, "YWJj", against the bytes read as UTF-8, "abc";
- INTERVAL: "1-2 3 4:5:6.5" against "1-2 3 4:5:6.500".
DATE, BOOL, INT64, other FLOAT64s, NUMERIC, BIGNUMERIC and RANGE agreed.

The patch writes those five in BigQuery's form when CAST's target is
STRING; ToString, the wire form, is unchanged. BYTES that are not UTF-8
are an error, and NULL with SAFE_CAST. Tests that held the old forms are
updated: five datetime specs and TestRegression_WindowOrderByNulls (a T),
and patch 0009's TestIntervalSignAndSubSecondParts ("1.5" is "1.500").

